The data moat

This is probably the most valuable part of the whole concept.

Most consumer beverage companies know:

what sold.

Beverage Goblin could eventually know:

why.

You’d accumulate an enormous beverage taste graph:

Person ↔ Drink ↔ Flavor ↔ Context ↔ Brand ↔ Store ↔ Price ↔ Location ↔ Social Group

So Beverage Goblin can discover things like:

People who love Baja Blast and Red Bull Juneberry have an unusually high probability of liking Product X.

Or:

This drink scores poorly overall but exceptionally well among endurance athletes.

Or:

Consumers love this flavor at $2.49 but purchase intent collapses above $3.19.

That’s incredibly useful market intelligence.

